<code>assert \forall int i; 0<=i && i<this.size(); this.contains(this.get(i)) => c.contains(this.get(i)));</code>

However, since `retainAll` removes elements not contained in `c`, the correct assertion should be that every element in the priority queue after `retainAll` is indeed in `c`. Here's the corrected version:

<code>assert \forall int i; 0<=i && i<this.size(); c.contains(this.get(i));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \forall int i; 0<=i && i<this.size(); c.contains(this.get(i)));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \forall int i; 0<=i && i<this.size(); c.contains(this.get(i)));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \forall int i; 0<=i && i<this.size(); c.contains(this.get(i)));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \forall int i; 0<=i && i<this.size(); c.contains(this.get(i)));</code>
--------------------
